WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.410 --> 00:00:01.640
(lively music)

00:00:01.640 --> 00:00:02.710
- [Narrator] The price of lithium

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.451
has been going through the roof.

00:00:04.451 --> 00:00:05.680
Why?

00:00:05.680 --> 00:00:07.070
Because it's the key ingredient

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:08.700
in rechargeable batteries used

00:00:08.700 --> 00:00:12.110
in everything from smartphones
to electric vehicles.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.930
And as governments and
companies increasingly move away

00:00:14.930 --> 00:00:16.810
from carbon-fueled economies,

00:00:16.810 --> 00:00:19.600
those batteries are in
higher demand than ever.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.883
- Traders and companies are betting

00:00:20.883 --> 00:00:23.100
that there won't be enough lithium supply

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.140
to meet demand in the years ahead.

00:00:25.140 --> 00:00:27.180
- [Narrator] There's actually
a lot of lithium available

00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:28.370
all over the world.

00:00:28.370 --> 00:00:31.690
Most current production comes
from Chile and Australia.

00:00:31.690 --> 00:00:34.660
While the extraction
process is relatively easy,

00:00:34.660 --> 00:00:37.960
converting it into battery-grade
chemicals is tough.

00:00:37.960 --> 00:00:40.837
Producers are also facing
environmental pushback.

00:00:40.837 --> 00:00:45.587
(protestor shouting in foreign language)

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:48.433
- [Narrator] These factors

00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:49.970
have electric vehicle makers worried

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.620
that they won't be able to
secure enough of the metal,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:54.420
and that could hinder the transition

00:00:54.420 --> 00:00:56.520
to a low-carbon future.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.960
- The future of
transportation in our nation

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.300
and around the world is electric.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:05.300
- [Narrator] As big automakers like Tesla,

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.790
Ford and General Motors
increase production

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:11.033
of electric cars, demand
for lithium is multiplying.

00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:14.260
Analysts expect the size
of the lithium market

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:16.870
to more than double by 2025.

00:01:16.870 --> 00:01:19.083
But right now, supply is tight.

00:01:19.960 --> 00:01:21.270
Once lithium is mined,

00:01:21.270 --> 00:01:23.400
which itself can take a long time,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.360
it's then sent to places like China

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.730
where the metal gets converted

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:28.860
into the chemicals needed for batteries.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.400
- China is the world leader

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.040
in processing these
battery-grade chemicals.

00:01:33.040 --> 00:01:34.660
So that's a major concern

00:01:34.660 --> 00:01:37.200
for US companies and politicians,

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:39.310
but you could also see
how shipping the stuff

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:42.810
all over the world creates a
very cumbersome supply chain.

00:01:42.810 --> 00:01:45.420
- [Narrator] Still, companies
and investors see lithium

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:47.080
as a huge market opportunity

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:50.230
as the transition to a
greener economy picks up pace.

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:51.510
- Because some people are saying

00:01:51.510 --> 00:01:54.920
that lithium could be the
21st century version of oil

00:01:54.920 --> 00:01:57.410
and that securing supply is so important,

00:01:57.410 --> 00:01:59.470
you see a lot of companies really trying

00:01:59.470 --> 00:02:01.260
to invest and produce,

00:02:01.260 --> 00:02:03.940
and that race is really
playing out everywhere

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:05.860
because again, lithium is abundant.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:08.580
It's just about getting
it out of the ground

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:10.580
and finding a kind of low-cost way

00:02:10.580 --> 00:02:12.610
and more sustainable way really

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:15.287
to convert it into
battery-grade chemicals.

00:02:15.287 --> 00:02:17.410
- [Narrator] As more
companies get involved

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:20.560
in lithium production,
analysts expect total supply

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:22.620
from countries like Australia and Chile

00:02:22.620 --> 00:02:24.220
to eventually exceed demand

00:02:24.220 --> 00:02:27.730
and cool the price rally in
the coming months and years.

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:29.710
Mining giant Rio Tinto is one

00:02:29.710 --> 00:02:32.880
of the many players getting
involved in the lithium market.

00:02:32.880 --> 00:02:36.910
The company recently
announced an $825 million deal

00:02:36.910 --> 00:02:39.103
to buy a lithium project in Argentina.

00:02:40.240 --> 00:02:41.710
But projects all over the world

00:02:41.710 --> 00:02:43.430
are being met with opposition.

00:02:44.473 --> 00:02:45.800
(crowd shouting)

00:02:45.800 --> 00:02:48.180
- In Serbia in December 2021,

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:50.260
we saw a lot of protests

00:02:50.260 --> 00:02:53.870
and thousands of protestors
in Belgrade blocking bridges

00:02:53.870 --> 00:02:56.270
to protest Rio Tinto's plans

00:02:56.270 --> 00:03:00.830
to invest over $2 billion
there for lithium production.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:02.020
- [Narrator] Environmentalists argue

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:04.400
that mining lithium can
require a lot of water

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.270
and that chemicals used in production

00:03:06.270 --> 00:03:08.120
can leak into nearby water supplies

00:03:08.120 --> 00:03:10.260
and harm the surroundings.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.050
- A Rio Tinto spokesman even told me

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.810
that they're not really going
to sacrifice the big picture

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.900
for local concerns.

00:03:17.900 --> 00:03:20.873
One reason some investors are
really bullish moving forward,

00:03:20.873 --> 00:03:23.700
if protestors and others concerned

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.100
about the environmental impact

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:28.130
won't let these companies
produce the commodities

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.570
that are needed to make
the electric vehicles,

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:32.970
then people see higher prices,

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.739
and supply scarcity and volatility ahead.

00:03:35.739 --> 00:03:38.489
(dramatic music)

